{
  "_comment": [
    "Per metric: op '>=' or '<=', 'target' (the goal: at or better is GREEN) and 'fail' (the regression line: worse than this is RED; between the two is YELLOW).",
    "target is where we want to be; fail was set just beyond the value MEASURED on 2026-10-15 so that the suite is a ratchet - a change that makes a number worse than today turns the build red, and a known gap shows as YELLOW with its failing examples printed.",
    "A metric with no entry here is shown as 'info' and never gates anything. A metric whose value is null is 'not run' and says why.",
    "15.10 - ratcheted after the fixes: category / confident-wrong / hallucination / timeout / graceful are now measured at their ceiling (100% / 0% / 0% / 0% / 100%), so fail sits AT the target - a fabricated confirmation or route, a hung tool, a raised tool that is not reported as failed, or a keyword matched inside another word turns the build red, not yellow.",
    "Timing thresholds leave a wide margin for shared CI runners; they catch an order-of-magnitude regression, not noise.",
    "Entries marked provisional (the live_* and rag_live.* ones) have NO measured baseline yet: they are the first guess and should be tightened after the first weekly run."
  ],

